      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shawn, once the auto toggle is enabled, PD_TASK will only loop around SNK_DISCONNECTED state but all of the existing code will be skipped, and the behavior I saw is that the CABLE_DET interrupt will trigger as soon as something is connect.\nIf a SNK is attached during this auto toggle, interrupt is triggered, TCPC-specific code in board.c will initialized TCPC and set Rd since PD_TASK is looping in SNK_DISCONNECTED, the tcpc_drp_state flag will be update so that the original SNK_DISCONNECTED is resumed, which will detect a SNK device is attached and move on to SNK_DISCONNECTED_DEBOUNCE.\nIf a SRC is attached, interrupt is triggered, same sequence will execute, and since we set to Rd, get_cc will return CC_OPEN, then will check if DRP is enabled. In S0 which DRP is set to manual toggle, it will transition to SRC_DISCONNECTED and detected the SRC. In S5 which DRP is set to force sink, it will just stay in SNK_DISCONNECTED, and when the counter is reached, enter back into auto-toggle/low power mode, but since CABLE_DET will remains high and it is only trigger on rising edge, it will not trigger again while the SRC continue to stay attached. In this case, a HOOK_CHIPSET_RESUME is added to force it to wake up if the system goes to S0.",
